# DeepCool MYSTIQUE AIO LCD (VID:PID 3633:0009)
#
# Vendor-specific USB device: no kernel driver is bound, libusb/pyusb claims
# interface 0 directly. The protocol uses endpoints 0x01/0x81 (init, info) and
# 0x02/0x82 (status, telemetry). See re/CONTEXT.md.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m 0644 99-mystique.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#   sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=usb
# then replug the AIO: udev applies rules when the device enumerates.
#
# Grant a group (recommended for a service account that is never logged in):
#   sudo groupadd -f plugdev
#   sudo usermod -aG plugdev "$USER"     # log out and back in
#
# Alternative for a single-user desktop, no group needed: replace the MODE and
# GROUP lines with
#   TAG+="uaccess"
# which lets systemd-logind grant an ACL to the user holding the active seat.
# The two are mutually exclusive in practice; use one.

SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="3633", ATTR{idProduct}=="0009", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev"
